Everyone's like, this guy's a genius.

88
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:10,720
He has figured out a way to transmute corn into cars.

89
00:23:10,720 --> 00:23:15,320
He's developed some kind of incredible Star Trek

90
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:17,240
Transformer array or something.

91
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:20,120
Until finally, a journalist sneaks from the factory

92
00:23:20,120 --> 00:23:22,280
and finds out it's just a dock.

93
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:24,400
And all that happens is Japanese cars come in,

94
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:26,640
or ships come in with cars.

95
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:28,520
And American trucks with corn go in.

96
00:23:28,520 --> 00:23:30,040
And they swap the corn in the cars.

97
00:23:30,040 --> 00:23:31,160
And they move out.

98
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:34,160
And then the journalist writes a story, corn into cars a fraud,

99
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,160
a lie.

100
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:37,660
And the guy gets arrested for violating all the international

101
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:38,200
trade laws.

102
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,800
The end.

103
00:23:39,800 --> 00:23:43,280
And the moral of the story, of course, is the scientist.

104
00:23:43,280 --> 00:23:45,840
Did the scientist have a technology

105
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:47,920
for turning corn into cars?

106
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:50,120
Of course he did.

107
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:52,600
Trade is the magical technology that

108
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:55,320
can turn anything into anything.

109
00:23:55,320 --> 00:23:57,080
The fact that a country called Japan even

110
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:58,880
exists with people in it is completely

111
00:23:58,880 --> 00:24:01,520
irrelevant from the American point of view.

112
00:24:01,520 --> 00:24:04,600
It might as just as well have been a big vat where

113
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:06,240
you throw in corn and cars come out,

114
00:24:06,240 --> 00:24:08,160
as far as Americans are concerned.

115
00:24:08,160 --> 00:24:11,400
It's the same thing, where it's just a technology

116
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:13,600
for taking stuff we have and turning it into something

117
00:24:13,600 --> 00:24:15,040
that we want more.

118
00:24:15,040 --> 00:24:17,480
And yet, very hard for people to accept

119
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:20,520
this way of looking at it.

120
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:22,280
And of course, from a human point of view,

121
00:24:22,280 --> 00:24:25,280
trade is better than just a technology.

122
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:29,480
Because with trade, there's a whole other country of people

123
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:31,360
who are benefiting also.

124
00:24:31,360 --> 00:24:33,880
Whereas just for a machine, where you pour in the corn,

125
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:36,400
turn the switch, and we burn up the corn and get a car,

126
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:37,160
it's good for us.

127
00:24:37,160 --> 00:24:38,920
But there's no one else benefiting.

128
00:24:38,920 --> 00:24:41,280
But this is actually where the corn goes someplace else.

129
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:43,320
And someone else gets to enjoy the stuff

130
00:24:43,320 --> 00:24:46,080
that, if it were just a machine, would have been burned up

131
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:48,240
in the process.

132
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:49,740
And of course, when you're thinking

133
00:24:49,740 --> 00:24:52,240
about what kinds of policies would any foreign buyers

134
00:24:52,240 --> 00:24:55,320
explain, well, all the policies designed

135
00:24:55,320 --> 00:24:59,720
to keep out foreign products fit very nicely here.

136
00:24:59,720 --> 00:25:02,000
Every time someone complains about countries selling us

137
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:05,400
