172
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:31,480
And this is phase one of a plan to destroy all the competition

173
00:26:31,480 --> 00:26:34,080
and then jack up the price to astronomical levels

174
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:36,240
when we have no other place to buy our books,

175
00:26:36,240 --> 00:26:38,880
rather than the obvious thing of, they're selling us cheap stuff

176
00:26:38,880 --> 00:26:42,240
and it's likely to continue or get better.

177
00:26:42,240 --> 00:26:45,120
All right, so and then, of course,

178
00:26:45,120 --> 00:26:47,800
immigration restrictions, one of my pet peeves,

179
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:51,520
explained very well by a deformed bias.

180
00:26:51,520 --> 00:26:54,000
Probably the strangest argument against immigration

181
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:55,560
that I've heard, and people, listen,

182
00:26:55,560 --> 00:26:56,600
there's one of the arguments people tell me,

183
00:26:56,600 --> 00:26:59,080
is they're like, Brian, you know what you don't understand?

