222
00:28:30,520 --> 00:28:32,840
Maybe even he's a wonderful thing.

223
00:28:32,840 --> 00:28:33,800
He enjoys life.

224
00:28:33,800 --> 00:28:34,600
He contributes.

225
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:36,480
What's the problem?

226
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:39,920
So anyway, that is my reaction.

227
00:28:39,920 --> 00:28:42,040
All right, many others disagree.

228
00:28:42,040 --> 00:28:43,520
All right, I'm writing a comic book,

229
00:28:43,520 --> 00:28:46,120
which will change all their minds.

230
00:28:46,120 --> 00:28:48,120
All right, then, your next figure,

231
00:28:48,120 --> 00:28:49,880
talking about network bias.

232
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:52,640
General tendency to evaluate economic performance

233
00:28:52,640 --> 00:28:55,200
based upon employment rather than production.

234
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:57,360
Very easy to make, especially during recession.

235
00:28:57,360 --> 00:29:02,080
Bodygate, if you just think about it

236
00:29:02,080 --> 00:29:04,480
in terms of basic principles that say, well,

237
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:06,920
was it bad that the tractor was developed?

238
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:10,360
Was it bad that all the labor saving agriculture machinery

239
00:29:10,360 --> 00:29:15,720
