00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:38,640
this would have sounded like the most naive, obtuse thing

250
00:29:38,640 --> 00:29:40,680
a human being has ever said.

251
00:29:40,680 --> 00:29:45,200
Because, look, agriculture is what 95% of human beings

252
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:47,840
have done for the last 10,000 years.

253
00:29:47,840 --> 00:29:50,040
And you think that we can eliminate almost all

254
00:29:50,040 --> 00:29:53,600
this employment and people will just find something else.

255
00:29:53,600 --> 00:29:56,640
But you refuse to identify or give any specifics on,

256
00:29:56,640 --> 00:29:58,600
and that's what will happen.

257
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:00,560
And yet, of course, that naive, obtuse thing

258
00:30:00,560 --> 00:30:02,600
was sensible advice.

259
00:30:02,600 --> 00:30:03,760
And there is a simple story.

260
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:07,080
Why was it that in 1840, it's hard to give specifics

261
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:09,440
about what all of the non-farmers

262
00:30:09,440 --> 00:30:10,840
are going to do with their lives?

263
00:30:13,880 --> 00:30:15,480
We've never been there before.

264
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:17,160
Like, you're going to say, well, they'll

