So, like, out of people who have never opened

368
00:54:09,000 --> 00:54:11,080
an economics textbook, I think it's fair to say

369
00:54:11,080 --> 00:54:12,720
90% are productionists.

370
00:54:13,960 --> 00:54:14,800
Right, and on the other hand,

371
00:54:14,800 --> 00:54:18,160
out of people who can correctly explain comparative advantage,

372
00:54:18,160 --> 00:54:20,720
which does not by itself imply agreement, right?

373
00:54:20,720 --> 00:54:22,760
Ideological Turing test, someone could go

374
00:54:22,760 --> 00:54:25,880
and perfectly explain it and then say it's all nonsense.

375
00:54:26,960 --> 00:54:29,120
But, out of people who can correctly explain

376
00:54:29,120 --> 00:54:31,200
comparative advantage, I think it's very fair to say

377
00:54:31,200 --> 00:54:33,200
90% of those people are free traders.

378
00:54:34,360 --> 00:54:37,440
Right, so what about a Pichetti economist like Peter Navarro?

