I don't know.

128
01:25:04,860 --> 01:25:06,460
I don't know.

129
01:25:06,460 --> 01:25:08,100
Maybe. I guess there might be a few.

130
01:25:08,100 --> 01:25:10,380
But I don't want to crush everybody.

131
01:25:10,380 --> 01:25:13,080
I suppose there might be some people there.

132
01:25:13,080 --> 01:25:14,240
I really hate crushing people.

133
01:25:14,240 --> 01:25:17,720
But I'm earning to give.

134
01:25:17,820 --> 01:25:20,760
I'm a football player and I give the money to the orphans.

135
01:25:21,440 --> 01:25:25,940
Anyway. So it seems like a really obvious control variable.

136
01:25:25,940 --> 01:25:27,580
But it does make people extremely angry.

137
01:25:28,700 --> 01:25:29,540
Now of course the fact

138
01:25:29,540 --> 01:25:31,520
that it makes people extremely angry doesn't mean it's a bad

139
01:25:31,520 --> 01:25:32,380
control variable.

140
01:25:32,380 --> 01:25:34,640
It could just be that they're very touchy.

141
01:25:35,300 --> 01:25:38,180
But there are actually several complaints that have been,

142
01:25:38,180 --> 01:25:39,700
that have been put forward.

143
01:25:39,700 --> 01:25:40,980
And so let's think about them.

144
01:25:41,540 --> 01:25:42,380
But anyway, just for background.

145
01:25:42,380 --> 01:25:43,780
So we all have an intuitive notion of what it means

146
01:25:43,780 --> 01:25:44,500
to be intelligent.

147
01:25:44,940 --> 01:25:46,320
If someone calls someone intelligent,

148
01:25:46,320 --> 01:25:48,360
you don't normally say what does that word mean.

149
01:25:48,360 --> 01:25:49,760
I have no idea what that word is.

150
01:25:49,760 --> 01:25:51,880
It's a perfectly normal English word.

151
01:25:52,320 --> 01:25:53,780
Found also in Dungeons and Dragons.

152
01:25:53,780 --> 01:25:55,740
It's one of the six primary characteristics along

153
01:25:55,740 --> 01:25:56,920
with strength, wisdom, dexterity,

154
01:25:56,920 --> 01:25:57,920
constitution, and charisma.

155
01:25:58,320 --> 01:25:59,840
And so clearly it means something, right?

156
01:26:00,260 --> 01:26:00,440
Right?

157
01:26:00,440 --> 01:26:01,640
All right.

158
01:26:02,260 --> 01:26:07,060
Now empirical research on intelligence is one

159
01:26:07,060 --> 01:26:08,840
of the best developed areas of psychology.

160
01:26:08,840 --> 01:26:12,400
Or actually I'll go and say it is the best developed area

161
01:26:12,400 --> 01:26:13,440
of empirical psychology.

162
01:26:14,060 --> 01:26:15,620
There is a massive amount of research

163
01:26:15,620 --> 01:26:17,380
on this topic in empirical psychology.

164
01:26:18,640 --> 01:26:18,840
All right.

165
01:26:19,340 --> 01:26:20,600
Now in practical terms,

166
01:26:20,940 --> 01:26:24,360
researchers usually measure intelligence with an IQ test,

167
01:26:24,360 --> 01:26:27,200
which stands for intelligence quotient, or related tests.

168
01:26:27,200 --> 01:26:31,000
There are many different tests which are not called IQ tests,

169
01:26:31,000 --> 01:26:33,440
but which are for all practical purposes IQ tests.

170
01:26:34,020 --> 01:26:37,120
Why are there so many tests that are IQ tests

171
01:26:37,120 --> 01:26:38,340
that aren't called IQ tests?

172
01:26:39,180 --> 01:26:41,000
Well, I've already hinted at what the reason might be

173
01:26:41,000 --> 01:26:41,620
to relabel them.

174
01:26:42,800 --> 01:26:43,900
Why relabel a test?

175
01:26:44,120 --> 01:26:45,140
Less controversial.

176
01:26:45,140 --> 01:26:46,420
Yes, to make people less angry.

177
01:26:46,980 --> 01:26:47,220
All right.

178
01:26:47,220 --> 01:26:50,640
Now my favorite example of this relabeling is the SAT,

179
01:26:51,060 --> 01:26:52,580
which when I was in high school stood

180
01:26:52,580 --> 01:26:54,220
for Scholastic Aptitude Test.

181
01:26:54,220 --> 01:26:59,180
Now that sounds a lot like intelligence, doesn't it?

182
01:26:59,180 --> 01:27:01,620
It's like, hmm, the student is super high

183
01:27:01,620 --> 01:27:03,380
in Scholastic Aptitude, but he's a moron.

184
01:27:03,380 --> 01:27:09,960
Or ultimately the student has no Scholastic Aptitude at all,

185
01:27:09,960 --> 01:27:11,060
but he's a complete genius.

186
01:27:11,060 --> 01:27:15,560
Hmm, sounds like a hard thing to imagine.

187
01:27:15,560 --> 01:27:18,600
I suppose you could, but it sounds odd.

188
01:27:19,080 --> 01:27:22,760
But anyway, a few years later the SAT test was

189
01:27:22,760 --> 01:27:27,740
not renamed, was not, the abbreviations stayed the same,

190
01:27:27,740 --> 01:27:29,700
but what the abbreviation was for changed.

191
01:27:30,100 --> 01:27:32,000
So it changed from Scholastic Aptitude Test

192
01:27:32,420 --> 01:27:36,240
to Scholastic Achievement Test to avoid hinting

193
01:27:36,240 --> 01:27:37,900
that someone might have an aptitude in anything.

194
01:27:38,260 --> 01:27:40,440
All right, because the idea of an aptitude, my God,

195
01:27:41,080 --> 01:27:42,880
once you say there's Scholastic Aptitude,

196
01:27:42,880 --> 01:27:46,020
there could be basketball aptitude or, you know,

197
01:27:47,320 --> 01:27:50,380
you know, acting aptitude or scuba diving aptitude

198
01:27:50,380 --> 01:27:51,400
or running aptitude.

199
01:27:51,400 --> 01:27:52,880
You don't want to say that, right?

200
01:27:52,880 --> 01:27:55,680
And then finally after a few more years that started

201
01:27:55,680 --> 01:27:59,280
to upset people, and then they renamed it to what it is now.

202
01:28:00,240 --> 01:28:01,780
What does the SAT stand for now?

203
01:28:02,100 --> 01:28:03,200
Nothing.

204
01:28:03,200 --> 01:28:05,460
They renamed it to nothing.

205
01:28:05,760 --> 01:28:07,340
It's just a name like Bob.

206
01:28:07,620 --> 01:28:09,300
So it's tasting, taking Bob.

207
01:28:09,300 --> 01:28:09,760
What does Bob say?

208
01:28:09,760 --> 01:28:10,820
Well, Bob doesn't say it for anything.

209
01:28:11,360 --> 01:28:14,960
So that was the sweet spot of avoiding controversy is

210
01:28:14,960 --> 01:28:16,840
to say your test doesn't stand for anything at all.

211
01:28:17,640 --> 01:28:20,060
But in any case, have you ever done, you know,

212
01:28:20,060 --> 01:28:22,940
is there's the Wechsler Intelligence Test or the Weiss

213
01:28:22,940 --> 01:28:25,880
or the Wunderlich or the SAT?

214
01:28:25,880 --> 01:28:30,380
Yes, the SAT is actually, correlates so highly

215
01:28:30,380 --> 01:28:32,200
with other tests that are called intelligence tests,

216
01:28:32,200 --> 01:28:33,520
it is an intelligence test.

217
01:28:33,920 --> 01:28:36,200
But the ETS doesn't want to be called an intelligence test.

218
01:28:36,640 --> 01:28:40,020
It might even sue me if I went out saying that too loudly

219
01:28:40,020 --> 01:28:42,480
and blatantly for labeling them.

220
01:28:42,480 --> 01:28:45,100
I guess it would be slander if I said it.

221
01:28:45,420 --> 01:28:45,920
All right.

222
01:28:45,920 --> 01:28:50,240
So in any case, these tests have come under angry attacks

223
01:28:50,240 --> 01:28:51,080
for a number of grounds.

224
01:28:51,080 --> 01:28:53,820
And we're just going to briefly go over the three main ones.

225
01:28:54,620 --> 01:28:54,880
All right.

226
01:28:54,880 --> 01:28:56,400
So the first complaint, cultural bias.

227
01:28:57,460 --> 01:28:57,620
All right.

228
01:28:57,620 --> 01:28:58,540
The origin of this complaint.

229
01:28:58,600 --> 01:29:01,220
There are large group differences in IQ scores.

230
01:29:02,000 --> 01:29:05,280
So Ashkenazi Jews, Jews of Eastern European ancestry,

231
01:29:05,620 --> 01:29:08,300
average about one standard deviation higher than Gentiles.

232
01:29:09,040 --> 01:29:11,380
Blacks average about one standard deviation lower

233
01:29:11,380 --> 01:29:12,720
than white Americans.

234
01:29:13,260 --> 01:29:14,220
I have nothing to do with this.

235
01:29:14,220 --> 01:29:15,920
This all predates me.

236
01:29:15,920 --> 01:29:17,800
Long before I was born, these numbers were there.

237
01:29:18,380 --> 01:29:18,880
All right.

238
01:29:18,880 --> 01:29:20,520
And out of people who know the data,

239
01:29:20,520 --> 01:29:22,000
there is no dispute about these numbers.

240
01:29:23,320 --> 01:29:24,460
The only question is why.

241
01:29:25,720 --> 01:29:26,200
Question is why.

242
01:29:26,320 --> 01:29:28,000
Why are there these large differences?

243
01:29:28,720 --> 01:29:30,240
And a common complaint is

244
01:29:30,280 --> 01:29:32,200
that the tests are culturally biased.

245
01:29:33,880 --> 01:29:35,000
Tests are culturally biased,

246
01:29:37,200 --> 01:29:39,720
which means that they don't really measure intelligence.

247
01:29:39,720 --> 01:29:41,960
They measure familiarity with middle

248
01:29:41,960 --> 01:29:44,280
or upper middle class lifestyles.

249
01:29:44,800 --> 01:29:49,560
Okay. Now, this argument was most notion back in the 50s

250
01:29:49,560 --> 01:29:52,600
where there were actually a few notorious questions on IQ tests

251
01:29:52,600 --> 01:29:54,640
with things like yacht is too big gata.

252
01:29:55,440 --> 01:30:00,720
As chalet is too big gata.

253
01:30:00,720 --> 01:30:04,160
Right now, as to how it was that kids from, you know,

254
01:30:04,160 --> 01:30:05,720
the Jewish kids from working class families

255
01:30:05,720 --> 01:30:07,340
in New York were being advantaged

256
01:30:07,340 --> 01:30:11,340
by these highly aristocratic references, I don't know.

257
01:30:11,340 --> 01:30:15,080
But, you know, anyway, there were some questions

258
01:30:15,080 --> 01:30:19,020
which you can go and find from this period which do sound,

259
01:30:19,020 --> 01:30:21,560
at least on the surface, to be about living

260
01:30:21,560 --> 01:30:23,200
in a very wealthy lifestyle.

261
01:30:23,200 --> 01:30:25,160
And so maybe they're not fair questions.

262
01:30:25,740 --> 01:30:30,460
But since then, not only have questions like that been removed

263
01:30:30,460 --> 01:30:32,480
from the test, and there's a lot of effort.

264
01:30:32,480 --> 01:30:34,780
Well, let's see, is there any way this could sound kind

265
01:30:34,780 --> 01:30:36,180
of like an upper middle class-y thing?

266
01:30:36,600 --> 01:30:38,740
But more importantly, people have come

267
01:30:38,740 --> 01:30:42,800
up with a very creative way of testing for cultural bias.

268
01:30:43,240 --> 01:30:45,980
And it's been done on a massive scale by the US military,

269
01:30:47,160 --> 01:30:50,260
which actually is the main organization on earth that uses

270
01:30:50,260 --> 01:30:54,100
IQ tests for making decisions about especially what kind

271
01:30:54,100 --> 01:30:55,540
of job they're going to train you for.

272
01:30:56,640 --> 01:30:59,960
All right, so I will tell you the theory of how you might go

273
01:30:59,960 --> 01:31:01,500
about testing your cultural bias,

274
01:31:01,500 --> 01:31:04,960
and then I will tell you what the tests wind up saying.

275
01:31:04,960 --> 01:31:11,100
All right, and just to give you a hint, this is one

276
01:31:11,100 --> 01:31:13,620
where people's intuition is usually exactly the opposite

277
01:31:13,620 --> 01:31:18,340
of the truth, so I will first go and tell you what you think,

278
01:31:18,340 --> 01:31:21,440
and then unless you are really, if you've got rational

279
01:31:21,440 --> 01:31:23,440
innovations, then you'll believe exactly what I'm going

280
01:31:23,440 --> 01:31:25,220
to tell you, but otherwise I'll have to fix it.

281
01:31:25,660 --> 01:31:28,380
Any case, so the way that people came up with

282
01:31:28,440 --> 01:31:30,220
for testing cultural bias is this.

283
01:31:30,820 --> 01:31:33,820
Let's go and on the x-axis get your IQ score.

284
01:31:33,820 --> 01:31:36,980
It could be scored in any paper and pencil test.

285
01:31:37,660 --> 01:31:43,240
All right, but then over here we're going to have a test

286
01:31:43,280 --> 01:31:46,400
of your practical performance, so like practical test performance,

287
01:31:48,400 --> 01:31:50,700
which if you're in the military, could be something

288
01:31:50,700 --> 01:31:52,800
like not crashing a plane.

289
01:31:53,900 --> 01:31:55,160
All right, now I trust you'll agree

290
01:31:55,160 --> 01:31:57,720
that there's nothing cultural about whether you crashed a

291
01:31:57,720 --> 01:31:59,200
plane or not, right?

292
01:31:59,620 --> 01:32:01,500
It is just an obvious fact

293
01:32:01,500 --> 01:32:02,820
about whether a plane's been crashed or not.

294
01:32:02,820 --> 01:32:05,300
It could, of course, be something less drastic

295
01:32:05,300 --> 01:32:09,200
like how many cones do you knock over when you were driving your

296
01:32:09,200 --> 01:32:10,360
tank through an obstacle course?

297
01:32:11,240 --> 01:32:12,820
Of course, you want to knock over no cones.

298
01:32:12,820 --> 01:32:14,820
You want to drive your tank perfectly through the course.

299
01:32:15,500 --> 01:32:19,020
So this could be any test of your skills.

300
01:32:19,020 --> 01:32:21,640
So this could be a medical test where you are,

